WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.838 --> 00:00:10.674
&gt;&gt;&gt; Starting February 15th the

00:00:10.774 --> 00:00:11.708
former president will have his

00:00:11.842 --> 00:00:13.043
first rival for the 2024

00:00:13.176 --> 00:00:14.344
presidential nomination.

00:00:14.678 --> 00:00:15.979
It's his one time ambassador and

00:00:16.113 --> 00:00:17.548
former South Carolina governor

00:00:17.681 --> 00:00:18.682
Nikki Haley.

00:00:18.682 --> 00:00:19.449
According to a force familiar

00:00:19.583 --> 00:00:23.120
with her plans, the invitations

00:00:23.253 --> 00:00:24.688
have already gone out and how

00:00:24.755 --> 00:00:27.324
she plans to set herself apart

00:00:27.457 --> 00:00:29.059
from a man she once criticized

00:00:29.192 --> 00:00:32.162
and broke with.

00:00:32.296 --> 00:00:33.697
&gt;&gt; We need to go in a new

00:00:33.830 --> 00:00:35.399
direction, and can I be that

00:00:35.532 --> 00:00:35.866
leader?

00:00:35.866 --> 00:00:39.636
Yes, I think I can be that

00:00:39.770 --> 00:00:40.103
leader.

00:00:40.103 --> 00:00:43.874
&gt;&gt; Reporter: Nikki Haley clearly

00:00:44.007 --> 00:00:44.975
hinting she was ready to launch

00:00:45.108 --> 00:00:46.376
her own presidential campaign in

00:00:46.710 --> 00:00:47.344
a recent interview.

00:00:47.477 --> 00:00:48.712
The former governor of south

00:00:48.712 --> 00:00:49.713
Carolina is poised to be the

00:00:49.846 --> 00:00:50.814
first Republican to challenge

00:00:50.948 --> 00:00:52.049
Donald Trump who launched his

00:00:52.182 --> 00:00:55.552
campaign last year.

00:00:55.686 --> 00:00:57.955
So far freezing out others from

00:00:58.088 --> 00:00:58.855
declaring their candidacy.

00:00:58.989 --> 00:01:00.290
&gt;&gt; We're going to win it, and

00:01:00.724 --> 00:01:01.558
we're going to win very big.

00:01:01.692 --> 00:01:05.062
&gt;&gt; Reporter: Making it for now a

00:01:05.195 --> 00:01:09.232
one-on-one match between two

00:01:09.366 --> 00:01:09.933
competitive politicians whose

00:01:10.067 --> 00:01:12.169
relationship has had many twists

00:01:12.302 --> 00:01:12.970
and turns.

00:01:13.103 --> 00:01:15.038
That was in the oval office in

00:01:15.172 --> 00:01:16.740
2019.
Haley was stepping down after

00:01:16.807 --> 00:01:18.275
serving for nearly two years as

00:01:18.408 --> 00:01:20.844
trump's ambassador to the united

00:01:20.978 --> 00:01:21.311
nations.

00:01:21.311 --> 00:01:23.847
But during the run up to his

00:01:23.981 --> 00:01:24.915
2016 campaign she was an

00:01:25.048 --> 00:01:26.216
outspoken critic.

00:01:26.350 --> 00:01:28.085
&gt;&gt; It can be tempting to follow

00:01:28.218 --> 00:01:30.754
the siren call of the angriest

00:01:30.787 --> 00:01:31.154
voices.

00:01:31.154 --> 00:01:33.924
We must resist that temptation.

00:01:34.057 --> 00:01:34.758
&gt;&gt; Reporter: Haley was

00:01:34.758 --> 00:01:36.760
especially critical of trump's

00:01:36.793 --> 00:01:37.527
proposal to put a temporary ban

00:01:37.661 --> 00:01:41.264
on muslims entering the U.S.

00:01:41.398 --> 00:01:43.734
&gt;&gt; It defies everything this

00:01:43.867 --> 00:01:44.768
country was based on.

00:01:44.901 --> 00:01:46.803
&gt;&gt; Reporter: And she ultimately

00:01:46.937 --> 00:01:48.405
chose to endorse Marco Rubio in

00:01:48.772 --> 00:01:49.406
the primary.

00:01:49.539 --> 00:01:50.774
&gt;&gt; I wanted somebody that had

00:01:50.907 --> 00:01:52.109
conviction to do the right

00:01:52.242 --> 00:01:52.742
thing.

00:01:52.776 --> 00:01:53.310
&gt;&gt; Reporter: But when trump

00:01:53.443 --> 00:01:56.146
became the nominee, Haley's tune

00:01:56.279 --> 00:01:56.780
shifted.

00:01:56.780 --> 00:01:58.782
&gt;&gt; The best person based on the

00:01:58.782 --> 00:02:01.118
policies and dealing with things

00:02:01.251 --> 00:02:03.120
like Obamacare still is Donald

00:02:03.253 --> 00:02:05.222
Trump.
That doesn't mean it's an easy

00:02:05.355 --> 00:02:05.656
vote.

00:02:05.656 --> 00:02:08.258
I did vote for him, and I was

00:02:08.392 --> 00:02:10.794
absolutely thrilled to see him

00:02:10.794 --> 00:02:15.999
win.
Get excited because I am just

00:02:16.133 --> 00:02:17.300
giddy.
&gt;&gt; Reporter: Her political

00:02:17.434 --> 00:02:19.436
skills were on display when she

00:02:19.569 --> 00:02:22.439
exited before trump's term was

00:02:22.806 --> 00:02:25.275
over before provoking him to

00:02:25.409 --> 00:02:25.842
chastise her.

00:02:25.842 --> 00:02:27.477
Haley shied away from rebuking

00:02:27.611 --> 00:02:29.446
trump when he refused to concede

00:02:29.579 --> 00:02:31.481
the 2020 election, but

00:02:31.615 --> 00:02:33.316
eventually she criticized him

00:02:33.450 --> 00:02:35.018
after January 6th telling

00:02:35.152 --> 00:02:36.420
politico, quote, we need to

00:02:36.820 --> 00:02:38.155
acknowledge he let us down, he

00:02:38.288 --> 00:02:40.490
went down a path he shouldn't

00:02:40.824 --> 00:02:41.925
have and we shouldn't have

00:02:42.059 --> 00:02:43.093
followed him, and we shouldn't

00:02:43.226 --> 00:02:44.394
have listened to him.

00:02:44.828 --> 00:02:46.930
And we can't let that happen

00:02:47.064 --> 00:02:49.700
again.
Then she appeared to repair any

00:02:49.833 --> 00:02:51.868
rift after the party signaled

00:02:52.002 --> 00:02:53.503
January 6th is not going to be

00:02:53.637 --> 00:02:55.338
the political end of trump.

00:02:55.472 --> 00:02:58.041
&gt;&gt; I would not run if president

00:02:58.175 --> 00:02:58.842
trump ran and I'll talk to him

00:02:58.909 --> 00:02:59.276
about it.

00:02:59.276 --> 00:03:00.444
That's something we'll have a

00:03:00.844 --> 00:03:02.846
conversation about at some point

00:03:02.846 --> 00:03:04.214
if that decision has to be made.

00:03:04.347 --> 00:03:08.085
&gt;&gt; Reporter: And trump says

00:03:08.218 --> 00:03:09.686
she's had to make that call.

00:03:09.820 --> 00:03:10.887
&gt;&gt; What's the strategy behind

00:03:11.021 --> 00:03:12.489
the timing of her announcement?

00:03:12.856 --> 00:03:14.091
Is there a reason this month?

00:03:14.224 --> 00:03:16.026
&gt;&gt; Reporter: Yeah, when you talk

00:03:16.159 --> 00:03:18.328
to Republican operatives they

00:03:18.462 --> 00:03:19.596
say this her opportunity for a

00:03:19.730 --> 00:03:21.231
moment in the spotlight,

00:03:21.364 --> 00:03:21.732
Anderson.

00:03:21.732 --> 00:03:22.499
Obviously she's going to be

00:03:22.866 --> 00:03:23.633
sharing that moment in the

00:03:23.767 --> 00:03:24.868
spotlight with former president

00:03:24.868 --> 00:03:25.635
trump, but it's going to give

00:03:25.769 --> 00:03:28.171
her an opportunity to get some

00:03:28.305 --> 00:03:29.239
sustained and focused attention

00:03:29.372 --> 00:03:30.874
from the media.

00:03:30.907 --> 00:03:32.008
We're doing stories on her right

00:03:32.142 --> 00:03:33.677
now and of course from voters

00:03:33.810 --> 00:03:34.945
who are paying attention this

00:03:35.078 --> 00:03:35.445
far-out.

00:03:35.445 --> 00:03:37.447
When you also talk to folks who

00:03:37.581 --> 00:03:41.818
are close to Nikki Haley it

00:03:41.952 --> 00:03:43.353
shows she's gutsy, she's

00:03:43.487 --> 00:03:44.888
determined, not scared to

00:03:44.888 --> 00:03:45.489
challenge trump and she's

00:03:45.622 --> 00:03:46.890
confident in herself.

00:03:46.957 --> 00:03:48.024
Of course there are drawbacks,

00:03:48.158 --> 00:03:50.193
too.
You talk to Republican

00:03:50.327 --> 00:03:51.795
operatives, some who plan to

00:03:51.928 --> 00:03:53.029
work for other folks or plan to

00:03:53.163 --> 00:03:56.166
get into the race and they say

00:03:56.299 --> 00:03:58.401
getting in this early could be

00:03:58.535 --> 00:03:59.236
dempmental because you're the

00:03:59.369 --> 00:04:00.504
only one the official punching

00:04:00.904 --> 00:04:02.906
bag for trump, and it gives him

00:04:02.906 --> 00:04:04.508
some sustained time to develop

00:04:04.908 --> 00:04:08.912
his critiques for Nikki Haley

00:04:08.912 --> 00:04:11.681
while it's this one-on-one race.

00:04:11.815 --> 00:04:14.084
&gt;&gt; The former chairman of the

00:04:14.217 --> 00:04:22.926
South Carolina Republican party.

00:04:22.926 --> 00:04:23.827
Chairman Dawson, good to have

00:04:23.960 --> 00:04:25.929
you on.

00:04:26.062 --> 00:04:26.930
So the former president is

00:04:26.963 --> 00:04:27.831
aralready knocking ambassador

00:04:27.964 --> 00:04:29.399
Haley posting on social media

00:04:29.533 --> 00:04:30.934
she's following her, quote,

00:04:30.934 --> 00:04:32.402
heart not her honor.

00:04:32.536 --> 00:04:34.237
Not sure exactly what that

00:04:34.371 --> 00:04:34.871
means.

00:04:34.938 --> 00:04:37.073
He's also posted an old clip of

00:04:37.207 --> 00:04:38.942
her saying she would not run if

00:04:38.975 --> 00:04:40.110
he ran again in 2024.

00:04:40.243 --> 00:04:42.946
What changed in her political

00:04:43.046 --> 00:04:43.980
calculus do you think?

00:04:44.114 --> 00:04:47.184
&gt;&gt; You've got to understand with

00:04:47.317 --> 00:04:49.886
Nikki Haley not much scares her.

00:04:50.020 --> 00:04:50.587
She's the most underestimated

00:04:50.954 --> 00:04:52.122
political candidate you'll ever

00:04:52.255 --> 00:04:54.958
see, and she has won races

00:04:54.958 --> 00:04:56.193
nobody thought she'd win.

00:04:56.326 --> 00:04:57.861
She's been the governor of the

00:04:57.994 --> 00:05:00.197
state of South Carolina, very

00:05:00.330 --> 00:05:00.830
popular.

00:05:00.964 --> 00:05:01.631
And I don't think Donald Trump

00:05:01.765 --> 00:05:02.966
scares Nikki Haley.

00:05:02.966 --> 00:05:04.100
I think she's been right in

00:05:04.234 --> 00:05:06.469
talking about this the next

00:05:06.603 --> 00:05:07.504
generation's time to serve.

00:05:07.637 --> 00:05:09.005
Right now you look at Joe Biden

00:05:09.139 --> 00:05:12.375
will be 82 years old if he's

00:05:12.509 --> 00:05:14.544
re-elected, Donald Trump will be

00:05:14.978 --> 00:05:15.712
78 years old, and there's going

00:05:15.846 --> 00:05:18.615
to be a contest for the

00:05:18.982 --> 00:05:20.050
presidency.

00:05:20.183 --> 00:05:21.685
Nikki Haley is just -- she's

00:05:21.818 --> 00:05:22.986
prepared herself.

00:05:22.986 --> 00:05:24.187
She's ready to get in, and she's

00:05:24.321 --> 00:05:25.689
ready to take it to Joe Biden

00:05:25.822 --> 00:05:27.557
and the administration where the

00:05:27.691 --> 00:05:28.425
country's failed us.

00:05:28.558 --> 00:05:29.860
And she's ready to give Donald

00:05:29.993 --> 00:05:30.994
Trump a contest.

00:05:31.027 --> 00:05:33.496
As to the rest of them to get

00:05:33.630 --> 00:05:35.298
in, jump in the water's fine,

00:05:35.432 --> 00:05:37.000
but Nikki Haley is in and she's

00:05:37.000 --> 00:05:38.535
going to run, and I think she's

00:05:38.668 --> 00:05:41.004
going to be very successful.

00:05:41.004 --> 00:05:43.006
&gt;&gt; How do you think she'll fare

00:05:43.139 --> 00:05:44.541
as a candidate?

00:05:44.674 --> 00:05:46.376
&gt;&gt; I'm a Nikki Haley fan.

00:05:46.509 --> 00:05:49.179
I think she's got the

00:05:49.312 --> 00:05:51.348
qualifications, a formidable

00:05:51.481 --> 00:05:51.848
candidate.

00:05:51.848 --> 00:05:53.016
She also needs to run directly

00:05:53.149 --> 00:05:53.950
against Donald Trump, and that's

00:05:54.084 --> 00:05:55.752
the open question is how willing

00:05:55.886 --> 00:05:57.187
she is to directly challenge him

00:05:57.320 --> 00:05:59.022
the by and large front-runner

00:05:59.089 --> 00:05:59.589
right now.

00:05:59.589 --> 00:06:01.024
Does she have the capability and

00:06:01.024 --> 00:06:04.494
the strengthen to do it, yes.

00:06:04.628 --> 00:06:05.495
The verdict is still out on

00:06:05.629 --> 00:06:07.030
whether she's actually willing

00:06:07.030 --> 00:06:09.032
to.
I think she's arguably the

00:06:09.032 --> 00:06:11.034
strongest candidate against him

00:06:11.101 --> 00:06:12.202
when she directly challenges

00:06:12.335 --> 00:06:12.835
him.

00:06:13.036 --> 00:06:14.104
The one caution I have is this

00:06:14.237 --> 00:06:15.772
is my cynical political take,

00:06:15.906 --> 00:06:17.040
there's one school of thought

00:06:17.040 --> 00:06:18.008
she's getting out early to

00:06:18.141 --> 00:06:19.476
actually ultimately run to be

00:06:19.609 --> 00:06:20.176
his vice president.

00:06:20.310 --> 00:06:21.778
I hope that's not the case.

00:06:21.912 --> 00:06:23.613
She has a record of her own to

00:06:23.747 --> 00:06:24.314
run on.

00:06:24.447 --> 00:06:25.048
She could be president tomorrow

00:06:25.181 --> 00:06:25.849
and be ready.

00:06:25.982 --> 00:06:29.819
&gt;&gt; One of the tests of that, I

00:06:29.953 --> 00:06:31.254
suppose, is whether she does

00:06:31.388 --> 00:06:32.289
directly take him on.

00:06:32.422 --> 00:06:33.657
&gt;&gt; The next couple of months

00:06:33.790 --> 00:06:35.692
will tell if that is her plan or

00:06:35.825 --> 00:06:37.761
truly a run for the presidency.

00:06:37.894 --> 00:06:39.663
&gt;&gt; Chairman Dawson, what about

00:06:39.796 --> 00:06:41.598
that?
We played in that clip that she

00:06:41.731 --> 00:06:43.767
did after January 6th say we

00:06:43.900 --> 00:06:46.036
shouldn't have gone down that

00:06:46.169 --> 00:06:49.639
road, we shouldn't follow him,

00:06:49.773 --> 00:06:51.675
we should never do it again.

00:06:51.808 --> 00:06:52.308
Do you think she will

00:06:52.375 --> 00:06:53.476
continue -- and then she kind of

00:06:53.610 --> 00:06:55.078
seemed to walk it back a little

00:06:55.078 --> 00:06:57.080
bit saying the things she said

00:06:57.080 --> 00:07:00.383
about never running if he was

00:07:00.517 --> 00:07:01.017
running.

00:07:01.084 --> 00:07:01.685
Do you think she will take on

00:07:01.818 --> 00:07:03.386
the former president directly?

00:07:03.520 --> 00:07:06.556
&gt;&gt; I know she'll him on it and

00:07:06.690 --> 00:07:08.358
be successful doing it.

00:07:08.491 --> 00:07:10.327
Nikki comes out of south

00:07:10.460 --> 00:07:11.094
Carolina.

00:07:11.094 --> 00:07:12.595
And, Anderson, you've been here

00:07:12.729 --> 00:07:13.096
before.

00:07:13.096 --> 00:07:13.663
This is a rough place.

00:07:13.797 --> 00:07:15.465
It's a place that this race is

00:07:15.598 --> 00:07:16.766
going to end up in the gutter,

00:07:17.100 --> 00:07:18.268
and we're going to have people

00:07:18.401 --> 00:07:19.102
in it.

00:07:19.102 --> 00:07:19.936
And the first one to come out

00:07:20.070 --> 00:07:21.438
and take a shower is going to be

00:07:21.571 --> 00:07:23.106
the winner, and that's probably

00:07:23.106 --> 00:07:25.508
going to be Nikki Haley.

00:07:25.642 --> 00:07:26.776
Donald Trump right now I think

00:07:27.110 --> 00:07:27.911
has hit his ceiling.

00:07:28.044 --> 00:07:28.678
We'll find out.

00:07:29.112 --> 00:07:31.114
He did a good -- a good small

00:07:31.214 --> 00:07:32.182
rally in South Carolina last

00:07:32.315 --> 00:07:34.050
week.
I would say trying to clear the

00:07:34.184 --> 00:07:36.119
field.
But this is going to be a

00:07:36.252 --> 00:07:36.586
contest.

00:07:36.586 --> 00:07:39.122
I think what Alissa's hitting on

00:07:39.155 --> 00:07:40.090
is how many people are going to

00:07:40.223 --> 00:07:41.591
be in it?

00:07:41.725 --> 00:07:44.594
Because as you know these crime

00:07:44.728 --> 00:07:46.596
areas are the winner takes all.

00:07:46.730 --> 00:07:51.935
So 31, 33% makes you a winner.

00:07:52.068 --> 00:07:54.504
So the question is are we going

00:07:54.637 --> 00:07:57.874
to a jungle primary with 16

00:07:58.008 --> 00:07:59.142
people in it, I don't think so.

00:07:59.209 --> 00:08:00.143
Who has the financial

00:08:00.276 --> 00:08:01.544
infrastructure to take on Donald

00:08:01.678 --> 00:08:02.112
Trump?

00:08:02.112 --> 00:08:03.146
Nikki Haley is one of those.

00:08:03.146 --> 00:08:05.148
She's prepared, we're excited

00:08:05.148 --> 00:08:07.283
about it, and we're going to

00:08:07.417 --> 00:08:08.118
have a contest.

00:08:08.251 --> 00:08:09.886
The Democrats maybe won't have a

00:08:10.020 --> 00:08:11.421
contest, but, boy, there's a lot

00:08:11.554 --> 00:08:12.489
going on in both parties right

00:08:12.622 --> 00:08:15.158
now about the generational shift

00:08:15.225 --> 00:08:17.494
that we see in the electoral

00:08:17.627 --> 00:08:19.429
village that we live in now that

00:08:19.562 --> 00:08:20.397
I think people are looking for

00:08:20.530 --> 00:08:22.465
the next generation to come

00:08:22.599 --> 00:08:24.000
cleanup what my generation

00:08:24.134 --> 00:08:25.301
couldn't get fixed and move us

00:08:25.435 --> 00:08:26.136
into a new place.

00:08:26.269 --> 00:08:28.138
&gt;&gt; Alyssa, chairman Dawson

00:08:28.271 --> 00:08:29.239
raised a good point.

00:08:29.372 --> 00:08:31.975
The more people who get in

00:08:32.108 --> 00:08:34.411
obviously good for -- for the

00:08:34.544 --> 00:08:35.845
political debate, but does it

00:08:35.979 --> 00:08:37.180
favor the former president?

00:08:37.180 --> 00:08:38.415
&gt;&gt; Yeah, the worst thing for the

00:08:38.548 --> 00:08:40.316
GOP would be to repeat 2016

00:08:40.450 --> 00:08:41.584
where you've got, you know, 16

00:08:41.718 --> 00:08:43.253
people on stage in two separate

00:08:43.386 --> 00:08:44.687
debates because you can't even

00:08:44.821 --> 00:08:45.955
fit them all up there.

00:08:46.089 --> 00:08:47.891
&gt;&gt; And the former president

00:08:48.024 --> 00:08:50.493
picks them off one by one.

00:08:50.627 --> 00:08:54.664
&gt;&gt; One by one and cannibalizes

00:08:54.798 --> 00:08:55.198
them.

00:08:55.198 --> 00:08:56.833
I think it's a show of strength

00:08:57.200 --> 00:08:58.001
if she's truly running against

00:08:58.134 --> 00:08:59.436
trump to go out early.

00:08:59.569 --> 00:09:03.206
It makes someone like a Mike

00:09:03.239 --> 00:09:05.542
pence or Mike Pompeo to

00:09:05.675 --> 00:09:06.042
consider.

00:09:06.042 --> 00:09:07.911
This is a woman who's next

00:09:08.044 --> 00:09:10.113
generation, she's a female that

